  "definition": "Momentum management keeps the angular momentum stored in spacecraft attitude actuators within a usable envelope. Reaction and momentum wheels exchange momentum internally with the spacecraft. They can reject a short disturbance or execute a slew, but cannot remove angular momentum from the closed spacecraft-wheel system. A persistent external torque therefore drives wheel speed and stored momentum towards a limit.[^nasa-actuators-2024]",
